## DESCRIPTION
## Compute arimetic operations between vectors.
## ENDDESCRIPTION


## DBsubject(Linear algebra)
## DBchapter(Matrices)
## DBsection(Matrix algebra)
## Date(September 5, 2011)
## Institution(Fitchburg State University)
## Author(Peter Staab)
## KEYWORDS('vectors', 'scalar', 'addition')

# updated 2022.12.12

DOCUMENT();    # This should be the first executable line in the problem.
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'MathObjects.pl', 'parserVectorUtils.pl',
    'PGML.pl');

Context('Vector');

$U = non_zero_vector3D(-5, 5, 1);
$V = non_zero_vector3D(-5, 5, 1);
$W = non_zero_vector3D(-5, 5, 1);

$k  = non_zero_random(-1, 1) * random(2, 5);
$k1 = random(2, 5);
$k2 = random(2, 5);

$v1 = $U+$V;
$v2 = $U+$W;
$v3 = $k*$U;
$v4 = $U-$V;
$v5 = $k1*$V+$k2*$W;

BEGIN_PGML

Suppose [` \vec{u} = [$U],  \vec{v} = [$V] `] and [` \vec{w}= [$W]`].

a) [` \vec{u}+\vec{v}`] = [____]{$v1}

b) [` \vec{u} + \vec{w} = `] [____]{$v2}

c) [` [$k] \vec{u} = `] [_____]{$v3}

d) [` \vec{u}-\vec{v} =`] [____]{$v4}

e) [`[$k1]\vec{v}+[$k2]\vec{w} `] [_____]{$v5}

Note: In this case, the vectors are written in the form of a sequence with angle brackets.  Your solution should have the same form.  Also, these operations are equivalent to those with either row or column vectors.

Enter vectors with < >.  [@ helpLink('vector') @]*
END_PGML



BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
In these cases, each operation is done element by element.  For example

a) [``` \vec{u}+\vec{v} = 
\begin{bmatrix} 
([$U->{data}[0]]) + ([$V->{data}[0]]) \\
([$U->{data}[1]]) + ([$V->{data}[1]]) \\
([$U->{data}[2]]) + ([$V->{data}[2]]) 
\end{bmatrix} = 
\begin{bmatrix} 
[$v1->{data}[0]] \\
[$v1->{data}[1]] \\
[$v1->{data}[2]]
\end{bmatrix}
```]
    Similarly, 
b) [``` \vec{u} + \vec{w} = \begin{bmatrix} 
[$v2->{data}[0]] \\
[$v2->{data}[1]] \\
[$v2->{data}[2]]
\end{bmatrix}
```]
c) [``` 5\vec{u} = \begin{bmatrix} 
[$v3->{data}[0]] \\
[$v3->{data}[1]] \\
[$v3->{data}[2]]
\end{bmatrix}
```]

d) [``` \vec{u} - \vec{v} = \begin{bmatrix} 
[$v4->{data}[0]] \\
[$v4->{data}[1]] \\
[$v4->{data}[2]]
\end{bmatrix}
```]

e) [``` 4\vec{v} + 3\vec{w} = \begin{bmatrix} 
[$v5->{data}[0]] \\
[$v5->{data}[1]] \\
[$v5->{data}[2]]
\end{bmatrix}
```]



END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();
